13
00:06:49,001 --> 00:06:51,841
Sousuke, come right back!

14
00:06:51,841 --> 00:06:52,631
Okay.

15
00:08:33,361 --> 00:08:34,481
A goldfish...

16
00:08:47,661 --> 00:08:48,871
It's stuck.

17
00:09:06,521 --> 00:09:07,681
That was weird.

18
00:09:18,281 --> 00:09:19,241
Ow!

19
00:09:22,411 --> 00:09:23,951
Is it dead?

20
00:09:28,041 --> 00:09:30,621
It licked me... It's alive.

21
00:09:33,331 --> 00:09:36,001
Sousuke, we're leaving!

22
00:09:36,001 --> 00:09:39,131
Lisa, I caught a goldfish!

23
00:09:49,641 --> 00:09:51,231
This wind feels strange...

24
00:09:51,231 --> 00:09:53,901
Sousuke, I'm starting the car!

25
00:10:03,111 --> 00:10:04,281
Did you find her?

26
00:10:09,951 --> 00:10:13,001
What? Captured by a human?

27
00:10:16,131 --> 00:10:18,461
This is bad... Very bad.

28
00:10:44,951 --> 00:10:46,661
Are you dead?

29
00:10:54,751 --> 00:10:55,961
You're alive!

30
00:11:05,471 --> 00:11:09,511
Sousuke! I'm going to be late!

31
00:11:09,931 --> 00:11:13,061
Lisa! I caught a goldfish.

32
00:11:13,061 --> 00:11:14,771
A goldfish?

33
00:11:14,771 --> 00:11:16,941
Down by the rocks.

34
00:11:42,921 --> 00:11:46,301
I'm sorry, but you can't use weed killer here.

35
00:11:48,881 --> 00:11:54,851
Heavens, no! This is pure sea water. It keeps me humidified.

36
00:11:54,851 --> 00:11:56,931
As long as it's not weed killer.

37
00:11:57,981 --> 00:11:59,061
Good day!

38
00:12:07,361 --> 00:12:09,411
This is very bad.

39
00:12:12,121 --> 00:12:13,951
What a creepy guy.

40
00:12:13,951 --> 00:12:17,291
But don't you say that about strangers, Sousuke.

41
00:12:17,291 --> 00:12:18,911
I won't.

42
00:12:18,911 --> 00:12:21,331
Are you taking that to school?

43
00:12:22,381 --> 00:12:23,921
Won't your teacher complain?

44
00:12:23,921 --> 00:12:28,131
Don't worry. I'll take care of you.

45
00:12:28,131 --> 00:12:29,631
She's cute!

46
00:12:36,471 --> 00:12:37,981
They're using the dry dock.

47
00:12:39,891 --> 00:12:42,191
Here. Eat this before we get there.

48
00:12:43,651 --> 00:12:45,611
Maybe she's hungry.

49
00:12:46,481 --> 00:12:47,611
Want some?

50
00:12:49,151 --> 00:12:51,281
Hey, my cut is gone!

51
00:12:54,621 --> 00:12:57,241
Lisa, I'm going to call her Ponyo.

52
00:12:58,121 --> 00:13:01,211
She's really special! She can do magic.

53
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:04,331
She fixed my cut.

54
00:13:14,641 --> 00:13:16,351
Want some ham?

55
00:13:31,651 --> 00:13:34,111
Lisa, Ponyo likes ham!

56
00:13:34,111 --> 00:13:35,621
That makes two of us.

57
00:13:59,141 --> 00:14:00,681
Oh, no...

58
00:14:03,481 --> 00:14:05,021
Disgusting!

59
00:14:05,021 --> 00:14:07,271
Hurry, Lisa-san!

60
00:14:15,991 --> 00:14:18,281
Such filth! Intolerable!

61
00:14:20,741 --> 00:14:22,291
Good morning!

62
00:14:28,841 --> 00:14:31,501
Look, Ponyo. There's our house.

63
00:14:41,011 --> 00:14:42,221
Morning.

64
00:14:53,231 --> 00:14:54,321
I'll drop you here.

65
00:14:54,321 --> 00:14:55,111
Okay.

66
00:14:55,111 --> 00:14:56,281
Have fun.

67
00:14:56,281 --> 00:14:57,861
See you.

68
00:14:59,241 --> 00:15:00,831
Morning. Sorry, I'm late.

69
00:15:00,831 --> 00:15:02,371
Could you get Noriko-san's wheelchair?

70
00:15:02,371 --> 00:15:03,411
Yes.

71
00:15:18,261 --> 00:15:20,051
Good morning, Sou-chan.

72
00:15:20,051 --> 00:15:22,971
I'm busy, Yoshie-san. Talk to you later.

73
00:15:22,971 --> 00:15:24,351
My!

74
00:15:24,351 --> 00:15:25,931
Hello, Sousuke-chan.

75
00:15:25,931 --> 00:15:27,481
Can't talk now, Toki-san.

76
00:15:27,481 --> 00:15:28,391
Oh, my.

77
00:15:35,531 --> 00:15:37,951
Maybe the teacher will get mad.

78
00:15:39,741 --> 00:15:40,701
I know!

79
00:15:44,871 --> 00:15:47,701
Wait here. I'll be back soon.

80
00:15:50,461 --> 00:15:52,251
What if a cat comes?

81
00:16:03,011 --> 00:16:06,601
Stay here. I'll be right back.

82
00:16:14,061 --> 00:16:16,361
See you later. Oh, hi, Toshi-chan.

83
00:16:18,441 --> 00:16:22,071
It's all right. She'll be just fine.

84
00:16:22,071 --> 00:16:24,241
Okay, thanks. Bye-bye.

85
00:16:24,781 --> 00:16:26,621
Good morning, Sensei.

86
00:16:26,621 --> 00:16:27,951
Hello Sou-chan.

87
00:16:27,951 --> 00:16:29,251
How are you?

88
00:16:34,631 --> 00:16:36,001
Sousuke!

89
00:16:36,001 --> 00:16:36,921
Kumiko-chan...

90
00:16:36,921 --> 00:16:40,301
Like my dress? Mommy got it for me.

91
00:16:40,301 --> 00:16:41,591
Oh...

92
00:16:41,591 --> 00:16:43,431
Let's play, Sousuke!

93
00:16:43,431 --> 00:16:45,641
Not now. I'm busy.

94
00:16:45,641 --> 00:16:47,311
How come?

95
00:16:47,311 --> 00:16:49,221
I told you, I'm busy.

96
00:16:49,221 --> 00:16:51,021
You're no fun.

97
00:16:51,021 --> 00:16:52,141
Yeah!

98
00:17:13,671 --> 00:17:14,871
Ponyo!

99
00:17:22,381 --> 00:17:23,881
Sousuke!

100
00:17:24,301 --> 00:17:25,221
Kumiko-chan...

101
00:17:25,221 --> 00:17:26,891
What's that?

102
00:17:26,891 --> 00:17:28,931
You're not supposed to bring stuff.

103
00:17:29,351 --> 00:17:33,521
But these trees aren't on school grounds, so that should be fine.

104
00:17:33,521 --> 00:17:34,771
Show me.

105
00:17:36,061 --> 00:17:37,691
Oh, a goldfish.

106
00:17:37,691 --> 00:17:40,071
It's not a goldfish. It's Ponyo.

107
00:17:40,071 --> 00:17:42,361
Ponyo? I want to see!

108
00:17:42,361 --> 00:17:44,821
Promise not to tell?

109
00:17:44,821 --> 00:17:46,111
I promise.

110
00:17:48,161 --> 00:17:50,121
Isn't she cute?

111
00:17:56,371 --> 00:18:00,091
It looks weird and fat. My goldfish is much cuter.

112
00:18:22,691 --> 00:18:26,901
It's Kumiko-chan's fault. She was mean to you.

113
00:18:30,741 --> 00:18:32,701
I'll give you some more water.

114
00:18:55,141 --> 00:18:56,101
Ponyo!

115
00:19:03,231 --> 00:19:04,111
You scared me.

116
00:19:09,451 --> 00:19:15,121
Why, how odd. That was Sousuke-chan's voice.

117
00:19:16,081 --> 00:19:20,331
But he's supposed to be in school.

118
00:19:20,331 --> 00:19:22,671
I must be hearing things.

119
00:19:22,671 --> 00:19:24,881
I'm here, Yoshie-san.

120
00:19:26,341 --> 00:19:29,971
I knew I heard your voice.

121
00:19:31,341 --> 00:19:33,721
Do I have a secret?

122
00:19:33,721 --> 00:19:34,721
Yes!

123
00:19:34,721 --> 00:19:35,851
Bingo!

124
00:19:36,561 --> 00:19:39,601
Okay, what color is my secret?

125
00:19:41,771 --> 00:19:43,651
Red!

126
00:19:44,061 --> 00:19:45,111
Good guess.

127
00:19:46,271 --> 00:19:48,571
How'd you know?

128
00:19:48,571 --> 00:19:50,071
Show us.

129
00:19:50,071 --> 00:19:50,781
All right.

130
00:19:53,911 --> 00:19:55,491
Oh, how pretty!

131
00:19:55,491 --> 00:19:57,241
Very cute!

132
00:19:57,241 --> 00:19:58,581
Her name is Ponyo.

133
00:19:58,581 --> 00:20:01,541
She loves ham and she can do magic.

134
00:20:02,541 --> 00:20:06,541
I cut my thumb, but she fixed it.

135
00:20:08,711 --> 00:20:12,511
I wonder if she'd fix our legs.

136
00:20:12,511 --> 00:20:16,551
We could run around just like you.

137
00:20:17,261 --> 00:20:20,811
Well, I'd have to ask Ponyo first.

138
00:20:20,811 --> 00:20:23,101
Can I take a look?

139
00:20:23,101 --> 00:20:24,441
Sure, Toki-san.

140
00:20:26,311 --> 00:20:29,611
Heavens, it has a face!

141
00:20:30,691 --> 00:20:34,991
Put it back before it brings a tsunami!

142
00:20:34,991 --> 00:20:38,161
You're so superstitious, Toki-san.

143
00:20:38,161 --> 00:20:41,621
That's what the old stories say.

144
00:20:41,621 --> 00:20:43,711
Fish like that are bad luck.

145
00:20:46,251 --> 00:20:49,051
The tsunami! It's here!

146
00:20:50,501 --> 00:20:52,211
The tsunami is here!

147
00:20:53,051 --> 00:20:54,431
Tsunami...

148
00:20:58,011 --> 00:20:59,561
What's wrong, Toki-san?

149
00:20:59,561 --> 00:21:02,061
Just look at my clothes!

150
00:21:09,981 --> 00:21:11,531
Sousuke!

151
00:21:16,321 --> 00:21:18,411
Sousuke!

152
00:21:20,831 --> 00:21:22,501
Sousuke!

153
00:21:24,251 --> 00:21:26,371
Sousuke!

154
00:21:26,371 --> 00:21:28,831
Come back here and apologize to Toki-san!

155
00:21:38,341 --> 00:21:42,141
Don't worry. I'll protect you.

156
00:21:44,101 --> 00:21:45,391
Sousuke...

157
00:21:48,941 --> 00:21:50,481
Sousuke...

158
00:21:54,651 --> 00:21:55,821
Ponyo!

159
00:21:58,281 --> 00:22:00,621
Ponyo... Sousuke...

160
00:22:01,281 --> 00:22:03,411
Ponyo... loves...

161
00:22:03,991 --> 00:22:04,911
...Sousuke!

162
00:22:10,961 --> 00:22:12,251
I love you too.

163
00:22:12,961 --> 00:22:15,341
Ponyo loves Sousuke!

164
00:22:56,211 --> 00:22:57,801
Ponyo!

165
00:22:59,011 --> 00:23:01,471
Ponyo!

166
00:23:02,721 --> 00:23:03,851
Ponyo!

167
00:23:06,181 --> 00:23:08,101
Ponyo!

168
00:23:09,481 --> 00:23:11,391
Ponyo!

169
00:23:09,771 --> 00:23:11,391
Sousuke!

170
00:23:13,151 --> 00:23:14,941
Ponyo!

171
00:23:15,441 --> 00:23:16,271
Ponyo!

172
00:23:16,691 --> 00:23:18,111
Ponyo!

173
00:23:18,111 --> 00:23:19,441
Ponyo!

174
00:23:21,111 --> 00:23:22,241
Ponyo!

175
00:24:16,831 --> 00:24:20,001
Listen, Sousuke. Maybe it was fate.

176
00:24:20,001 --> 00:24:22,261
It just can't be helped.

177
00:24:23,171 --> 00:24:25,471
Ponyo was born in the sea.

178
00:24:25,471 --> 00:24:27,341
She went back home. That's all.

179
00:24:27,891 --> 00:24:31,021
Anyway, let's hope that creepy guy is gone.

180
00:24:32,641 --> 00:24:33,731
One lick?

181
00:24:34,851 --> 00:24:36,231
Hurry, it's melting!

182
00:24:39,651 --> 00:24:41,031
Not bad!

183
00:24:46,161 --> 00:24:49,491
Cheer up. Koichi will be home tonight.

184
00:24:50,621 --> 00:24:53,411
He'll be disappointed if you're feeling down.

185
00:25:19,861 --> 00:25:22,111
No more ocean today, okay?

186
00:25:49,431 --> 00:25:50,511
Sousuke?

187
00:25:51,851 --> 00:25:53,431
Time to come inside.

188
00:25:53,931 --> 00:25:58,441
Do you think this bucket will help Ponyo find us?

189
00:25:58,851 --> 00:26:01,941
There's only one way to find out.

190
00:26:16,041 --> 00:26:19,461
Can you get that, Sousuke? It must be Koichi.

191
00:26:21,961 --> 00:26:23,331
Hello?

192
00:26:23,331 --> 00:26:25,131
Yes, it's me.

193
00:26:25,841 --> 00:26:27,921
Yes, I'm fine.

194
00:26:27,921 --> 00:26:32,261
I can't get back tonight. I'll signal when I'm offshore.

195
00:26:32,261 --> 00:26:34,551
Okay. Here's Lisa.

196
00:26:36,311 --> 00:26:39,981
Koichi? Yes... What?!

197
00:26:39,981 --> 00:26:42,351
Can't you get out of it?

198
00:26:42,351 --> 00:26:46,191
Fine... Leave your wife and son up on the cliff!

199
00:26:46,191 --> 00:26:47,611
I give up!

200
00:26:51,451 --> 00:26:53,361
Why bother?

201
00:26:53,361 --> 00:26:55,451
C'mon, Sousuke. Let's eat out!

202
00:26:56,581 --> 00:26:58,291
I want to eat here.

203
00:27:27,271 --> 00:27:28,151
There he is!

204
00:27:28,151 --> 00:27:30,991
Turn off the lights, Lisa.

205
00:27:54,881 --> 00:27:59,011
It's Sousuke! He's a genius. Only five years old.

206
00:27:59,011 --> 00:28:00,891
Your wife must be upset.

207
00:28:05,481 --> 00:28:09,361
He says he's sorry.

