267
00:28:58,781 --> 00:29:01,661
LOVE AND KISSES

268
00:29:19,431 --> 00:29:21,641
Don't cry, Lisa.

269
00:29:22,681 --> 00:29:24,221
I won't cry.

270
00:29:25,641 --> 00:29:29,391
I promised Ponyo, I'd take care of her.

271
00:29:34,021 --> 00:29:36,611
I hope she isn't crying.

272
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:43,411
Okay, let's cheer up!

273
00:29:44,371 --> 00:29:47,121
"I'm happy as can be..."

274
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:49,461
Ow!

275
00:29:49,461 --> 00:29:51,081
Don't worry, Sousuke.

276
00:29:51,081 --> 00:29:54,131
I'm sure Ponyo is fine too.

277
00:29:57,051 --> 00:30:01,051
Now, let's eat. We'll eat Koichi's dinner too!

278
00:30:10,851 --> 00:30:12,561
This is all my fault.

279
00:30:12,561 --> 00:30:17,191
Bringing you along to watch me was a mistake.

280
00:30:17,901 --> 00:30:21,281
How often have I warned you about humans?

281
00:30:21,281 --> 00:30:23,361
Their very breath is polluted.

282
00:30:23,911 --> 00:30:26,281
Come, you must eat.

283
00:30:26,281 --> 00:30:28,371
Can't you hear me, Brunhilde?

284
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:31,291
I want ham!

285
00:30:33,711 --> 00:30:37,801
H-Ham?! What on earth have you been doing?

286
00:30:37,801 --> 00:30:39,841
Answer me, Brunhilde!

287
00:30:39,841 --> 00:30:43,181
My name's not Brunhilde. It's Ponyo.

288
00:30:43,181 --> 00:30:45,181
Ponyo?

289
00:30:45,181 --> 00:30:47,971
Ponyo loves Sousuke.

290
00:30:47,971 --> 00:30:50,981
I want to be human!

291
00:30:51,481 --> 00:30:52,941
Human?

292
00:30:52,941 --> 00:30:55,811
How could you love such disgusting creatures?

293
00:30:56,611 --> 00:30:59,401
They rob the sea of life.

294
00:31:00,151 --> 00:31:02,741
I was human myself... once.

295
00:31:03,281 --> 00:31:05,821
I finally escaped that awful heritage...

296
00:31:05,821 --> 00:31:08,031
I want hands!

297
00:31:08,701 --> 00:31:11,161
I don't like this!

298
00:31:12,001 --> 00:31:15,041
I want legs like Sousuke!

299
00:31:15,041 --> 00:31:16,461
Of all the nonsense!

300
00:31:35,941 --> 00:31:39,401
Look at me! Hands and feet!

301
00:31:39,981 --> 00:31:40,771
Look at me!

302
00:31:40,771 --> 00:31:44,741
No... Don't tell me you tasted human blood?!

303
00:31:44,741 --> 00:31:46,281
Wanna see Sousuke!

304
00:31:46,281 --> 00:31:50,331
No! His blood has deranged your DNA!

305
00:31:50,331 --> 00:31:53,501
Revert... Revert...

306
00:31:58,751 --> 00:32:01,711
Go back... Go back!

307
00:32:05,591 --> 00:32:07,801
It's not working. I need more power.

308
00:32:21,481 --> 00:32:22,691
Let me out!

309
00:32:22,691 --> 00:32:26,111
Be still, you evil blood.

310
00:32:26,111 --> 00:32:28,951
Revert, revert!

311
00:32:38,211 --> 00:32:42,001
Just like her mother... So strong.

312
00:32:47,221 --> 00:32:50,221
She should remain innocent and pure forever.

313
00:33:11,411 --> 00:33:14,491
I can't hold her for long.

314
00:33:14,491 --> 00:33:17,041
I need her mother's help.

315
00:33:26,341 --> 00:33:28,881
No! My elixir is too strong for you!

316
00:33:29,551 --> 00:33:31,551
Shoo! Go away!

317
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:35,051
My crab shields were weakening.

318
00:33:35,051 --> 00:33:37,311
I nearly upset Nature's balance.

319
00:33:37,311 --> 00:33:38,681
I must stay calm.

320
00:33:38,681 --> 00:33:42,521
When I think of meeting her again, I'm starting to get nervous.

321
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:45,861
This batch should be ready.

322
00:33:55,121 --> 00:33:56,911
No leaks down here.

323
00:34:01,541 --> 00:34:03,331
This door is loose.

324
00:34:08,631 --> 00:34:10,131
I'll fix it later.

325
00:34:17,181 --> 00:34:19,471
If even one creature got in here...

326
00:34:43,711 --> 00:34:45,251
Superb!

327
00:34:45,251 --> 00:34:49,801
I feel the ocean's power in my very DNA.

328
00:34:50,421 --> 00:34:54,841
When this well is full, the Era of the Ocean will begin.

329
00:34:54,841 --> 00:34:58,051
An explosion of life to match the Cambrian Era!

330
00:34:58,051 --> 00:35:00,681
This revolting era of Man will be over.

331
00:35:05,851 --> 00:35:07,481
Better fix this door.

332
00:36:31,601 --> 00:36:33,061
Teeth!

333
00:36:41,071 --> 00:36:43,201
I'm going back to Sousuke!

334
00:39:14,471 --> 00:39:15,731
A waterspout?

335
00:39:15,731 --> 00:39:17,981
Captain, look there!

336
00:39:21,191 --> 00:39:22,691
Tsunami!

337
00:39:22,691 --> 00:39:24,611
Turn her into the waves!

338
00:39:26,281 --> 00:39:27,821
What's that?

339
00:39:32,701 --> 00:39:35,791
Captain, the radio's out! The radar too!

340
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:42,921
A little girl? She must be Sousuke's age!

341
00:39:52,891 --> 00:39:55,101
Bye-bye. See you tomorrow.

342
00:39:56,721 --> 00:39:59,521
Thanks. Take care.

343
00:40:00,691 --> 00:40:04,021
Sou-chan, do you want to wait here together?

344
00:40:04,021 --> 00:40:05,941
It's okay. I'll take the shortcut.

345
00:40:05,941 --> 00:40:07,441
Goodbye, Sensei.

346
00:40:07,441 --> 00:40:08,821
Goodbye.

347
00:40:09,361 --> 00:40:10,701
Be careful out there.

348
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:56,871
Sorry, Sousuke. The door wouldn't open, right?

349
00:40:56,871 --> 00:40:58,371
The power's out.

350
00:40:58,371 --> 00:40:59,831
Was the school okay?

351
00:41:00,291 --> 00:41:03,831
Lisa-san, we'll be fine. Go home.

352
00:41:03,831 --> 00:41:05,541
Are you sure?

353
00:41:05,541 --> 00:41:07,961
Don't worry. We'll be just fine.

354
00:41:08,341 --> 00:41:13,511
We're spending the night anyway. You should go while you can.

355
00:41:14,931 --> 00:41:16,931
Wait for me, Sousuke.

356
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:30,071
Yoshie-san...

357
00:41:30,901 --> 00:41:35,821
Why, Sou-chan... It's so dark, I didn't see you.

358
00:41:35,821 --> 00:41:38,121
This is for you.

359
00:41:40,581 --> 00:41:43,621
My, what is it?

360
00:41:43,621 --> 00:41:45,461
One for you, Noriko-san.

361
00:41:45,461 --> 00:41:47,171
Thank you.

362
00:41:47,171 --> 00:41:49,501
Can't see a thing.

363
00:41:49,501 --> 00:41:52,511
This is such foolishness!

364
00:41:52,511 --> 00:41:55,381
I don't want to spend the night.

365
00:41:58,891 --> 00:42:00,011
The power's on.

366
00:42:00,011 --> 00:42:00,851
Oh, good.

367
00:42:00,851 --> 00:42:02,771
Certainly is.

368
00:42:02,771 --> 00:42:04,061
It's a goldfish!

369
00:42:04,061 --> 00:42:08,561
Maybe Sou-chan's magic made the lights go on?

370
00:42:08,561 --> 00:42:11,571
Extremely powerful... Micro typhoon...

371
00:42:11,571 --> 00:42:14,031
Ships should exercise extreme caution...

372
00:42:15,361 --> 00:42:17,281
This TV is useless.

373
00:42:17,281 --> 00:42:22,491
Those idiots couldn't forecast their way out of a paper bag.

374
00:42:22,491 --> 00:42:24,541
You should go home, Sou-chan.

375
00:42:25,001 --> 00:42:27,461
Your goldfish will bring us luck.

376
00:42:27,461 --> 00:42:29,881
We're not afraid anymore.

377
00:42:38,551 --> 00:42:40,141
Here's yours, Toki-san.

378
00:42:44,061 --> 00:42:46,101
It's all wrinkled.

379
00:42:46,101 --> 00:42:47,731
What is it?

380
00:42:47,731 --> 00:42:48,651
Like this.

381
00:42:51,231 --> 00:42:53,231
I know! It's a grasshopper.

382
00:42:53,231 --> 00:42:55,611
No, the Koganei Maru.

383
00:42:55,611 --> 00:42:58,821
That's your father's ship, isn't it?

384
00:42:59,531 --> 00:43:01,701
Still looks like a grasshopper.

385
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:06,001
We're leaving, Sousuke. Say goodbye to everyone.

386
00:43:08,161 --> 00:43:10,541
Goodbye, everybody.

387
00:43:10,541 --> 00:43:12,591
Goodbye.

388
00:43:13,291 --> 00:43:15,761
Don't let the wind blow you away!

389
00:43:16,761 --> 00:43:18,171
Climb over.

390
00:43:23,101 --> 00:43:24,811
The phones are out too.

391
00:43:48,621 --> 00:43:50,501
The sea is puffed up!

392
00:43:54,591 --> 00:43:56,921
Will the ships sink?

393
00:43:57,421 --> 00:44:00,221
They're safe out at sea.

394
00:44:00,221 --> 00:44:01,931
I'm sure that's where Koichi is.

395
00:44:13,271 --> 00:44:15,861
I see fish, Lisa.

396
00:44:15,861 --> 00:44:17,111
Fasten your seatbelt!

397
00:44:27,871 --> 00:44:30,251
You've got to turn back!

398
00:44:30,251 --> 00:44:33,171
People are going to the shelters.

399
00:44:33,171 --> 00:44:37,631
But there are people at the senior center!

400
00:44:37,631 --> 00:44:41,721
They'll be all right. They're on the leeward side.

401
00:44:42,301 --> 00:44:45,341
I've just got to get home.

402
00:44:45,341 --> 00:44:47,801
You'd better go around the mountain.

403
00:44:50,971 --> 00:44:52,731
Here we go, Sousuke.

404
00:44:54,061 --> 00:44:55,651
No! Stop!

405
00:44:55,651 --> 00:44:57,361
Look out for that wave!

406
00:45:02,941 --> 00:45:04,241
Here it comes!

407
00:45:04,241 --> 00:45:06,411
Run for it, Lisa-san!

408
00:45:46,531 --> 00:45:48,071
The fish are following us.

409
00:45:48,071 --> 00:45:49,621
Fasten your seatbelt, Sousuke!

410
00:46:03,341 --> 00:46:05,011
Hold on tight!

411
00:46:57,271 --> 00:46:58,931
That wave won't quit!

412
00:47:09,321 --> 00:47:11,201
A little girl fell in.

413
00:47:11,661 --> 00:47:13,321
She was riding a fish.

414
00:47:18,411 --> 00:47:19,541
Where?

415
00:47:28,711 --> 00:47:30,301
The sea keeps rising.

416
00:47:30,301 --> 00:47:32,721
Where did you see her?

417
00:47:32,721 --> 00:47:35,761
Running on top of a fish.

418
00:47:35,761 --> 00:47:36,811
A fish?!

419
00:47:41,481 --> 00:47:42,731
Come on, Sousuke.

420
00:47:58,541 --> 00:48:02,121
Hang on, Sousuke! We're almost home.

421
00:48:56,301 --> 00:48:58,051
A little girl!

422
00:48:58,051 --> 00:49:00,891
It's dangerous out here. You'd better come with us.

423
00:49:01,561 --> 00:49:03,221
Stay there, Sousuke.

424
00:49:29,041 --> 00:49:31,131
Sousuke, do you know her?

425
00:49:52,521 --> 00:49:53,771
Ponyo?

426
00:49:54,691 --> 00:49:56,941
Yes, it's me!

427
00:49:57,191 --> 00:49:58,361
It's you!

428
00:50:00,281 --> 00:50:04,031
Ponyo's a little girl now, Lisa!

429
00:50:15,671 --> 00:50:17,841
I made it!

430
00:50:36,021 --> 00:50:39,151
Now listen, children.

431
00:50:39,151 --> 00:50:42,991
No matter how strange everything seems...

432
00:50:42,991 --> 00:50:45,201
...we have to stay calm, all right?

433
00:50:46,201 --> 00:50:47,201
Now be good.

434
00:50:51,211 --> 00:50:53,541
Take off your rain coat, Sousuke.

435
00:50:53,921 --> 00:50:56,551
Here, Ponyo. You hold the light.

436
00:51:01,221 --> 00:51:03,341
I'll bring you a towel.

437
00:51:20,491 --> 00:51:21,741
C'mon, Ponyo!

438
00:51:24,111 --> 00:51:26,241
It smells just like you!

439
00:51:28,991 --> 00:51:29,911
Ouch!

440
00:51:29,911 --> 00:51:30,751
Ponyo!

441
00:51:35,631 --> 00:51:39,381
Gotcha! Let's get you dried off.

442
00:51:43,431 --> 00:51:45,891
Such pretty red hair!

443
00:51:48,721 --> 00:51:50,181
But your clothes are dry...

444
00:51:50,681 --> 00:51:53,181
Ponyo was a fish.

445
00:51:53,181 --> 00:51:54,691
Water doesn't make her wet.

446
00:51:58,311 --> 00:52:00,191
I like this!

447
00:52:00,191 --> 00:52:03,701
All right! Who wants a hot drink?

448
00:52:03,701 --> 00:52:06,411
Help me with the light, Ponyo.

449
00:52:06,411 --> 00:52:08,201
Coming!

450
00:52:08,201 --> 00:52:10,331
Think we'll have water?

451
00:52:10,331 --> 00:52:11,541
Sure!

452
00:52:11,541 --> 00:52:12,831
Sure!

453
00:52:15,921 --> 00:52:16,581
Water!

454
00:52:16,581 --> 00:52:17,881
Water!

455
00:52:18,961 --> 00:52:21,591
We have a tank outside.

456
00:52:23,261 --> 00:52:25,681
What about the gas?

457
00:52:25,681 --> 00:52:26,431
Presto!

458
00:52:27,181 --> 00:52:27,931
All right!

459
00:52:27,931 --> 00:52:29,351
All right!

460
00:52:29,351 --> 00:52:31,311
It's propane.

461
00:52:33,851 --> 00:52:35,731
Okay, take your seats.

462
00:52:36,521 --> 00:52:37,851
Okay!

463
00:52:37,851 --> 00:52:39,561
Over here, Ponyo.

464
00:52:45,571 --> 00:52:47,031
Sit down like this.

465
00:52:50,281 --> 00:52:51,911
Put your stuff down.

466
00:52:54,411 --> 00:52:56,371
You need your hands.

467
00:52:56,371 --> 00:52:57,831
I have feet!

468
00:53:00,751 --> 00:53:02,041
Wow!

469
00:53:05,211 --> 00:53:07,261
What are you two doing?

470
00:53:07,261 --> 00:53:09,891
Her feet are like hands.

471
00:53:29,821 --> 00:53:30,821
There you go.

472
00:53:32,741 --> 00:53:33,491
One for you.

473
00:53:38,831 --> 00:53:40,371
Thanks for the tea!

474
00:54:28,881 --> 00:54:30,381
That was delicious.

475
00:54:31,341 --> 00:54:34,301
What shall we do now?

476
00:54:34,721 --> 00:54:36,471
I want ham!

477
00:54:36,471 --> 00:54:38,431
She's crazy about ham.

478
00:54:40,141 --> 00:54:42,441
Then let's eat.

479
00:54:42,441 --> 00:54:45,401
But first let's start the generator.

480
00:54:46,731 --> 00:54:49,861
We need electricity to talk to Koichi.

481
00:54:50,991 --> 00:54:53,661
Koichi is my father.

482
00:54:53,661 --> 00:54:55,491
Is he a bad sorcerer?

483
00:54:55,491 --> 00:54:58,951
No, he's a ship captain.

484
00:54:59,621 --> 00:55:01,581
What about your father, Ponyo?

485
00:55:01,581 --> 00:55:04,871
Fujimoto! He keeps me prisoner.

486
00:55:05,881 --> 00:55:08,041
I ran away.

487
00:55:09,591 --> 00:55:11,211
What about your mother?

488
00:55:11,211 --> 00:55:15,051
I love my mother!

489
00:55:15,051 --> 00:55:17,801
She's really scary.

490
00:55:17,801 --> 00:55:19,101
Sounds like Lisa.

491
00:55:24,141 --> 00:55:25,771
Can you help me, Ponyo?

492
00:55:43,121 --> 00:55:44,831
Maybe the fuel's too old?

493
00:55:45,331 --> 00:55:46,831
Is it clogged?

494
00:55:46,831 --> 00:55:47,961
Clogged.

495
00:55:47,961 --> 00:55:50,341
It's clogged there.

496
00:56:05,021 --> 00:56:06,641
Success!

497
00:56:07,061 --> 00:56:08,521
All bright!

498
00:56:10,561 --> 00:56:11,901
Wow, Ponyo!

499
00:56:30,331 --> 00:56:32,251
Antenna! Antenna!

500
00:56:32,251 --> 00:56:35,261
Did all the ships sink, Lisa?

501
00:56:36,591 --> 00:56:38,431
I can't see a single light.

502
00:56:56,741 --> 00:56:58,781
So loud!

503
00:56:58,781 --> 00:56:59,741
What's wrong?

504
00:57:00,821 --> 00:57:03,371
Even the radio is out of whack.

505
00:57:04,491 --> 00:57:08,751
This is JA4LL... JA4LL.

506
00:57:08,751 --> 00:57:11,001
Come in, Koichi.

507
00:57:11,001 --> 00:57:15,341
It's Lisa, Sousuke and Ponyo. We're all doing fine.

508
00:57:16,671 --> 00:57:18,801
We're going to have dinner.

509
00:57:19,381 --> 00:57:20,761
Ham!

510
00:57:29,561 --> 00:57:32,601
Ready? Be careful. It's hot.

511
00:57:48,791 --> 00:57:50,711
It's not ready yet.

512
00:57:50,711 --> 00:57:52,121
It takes three minutes.

513
00:58:07,351 --> 00:58:09,351
Close your eyes!

514
00:58:09,971 --> 00:58:11,351
Not yet!

515
00:58:13,901 --> 00:58:15,521
No peeking, Ponyo.

516
00:58:19,531 --> 00:58:21,531
Okay, you can look now.

517
00:58:22,321 --> 00:58:24,911
And... presto!

518
00:58:30,911 --> 00:58:32,121
Ham!

519
00:58:32,121 --> 00:58:33,661
Good for you, Ponyo.

520
00:58:55,101 --> 00:58:57,061
Lisa, Ponyo fell asleep.

521
00:59:04,401 --> 00:59:06,861
Is her home far away?

522
00:59:06,861 --> 00:59:08,571
I think it must be.

523
00:59:24,551 --> 00:59:27,261
Look, Sousuke. The sea is calmer.

524
00:59:28,341 --> 00:59:30,011
Because Ponyo's asleep?

525
00:59:30,011 --> 00:59:31,561
Look over there!

526
00:59:39,521 --> 00:59:42,571
It's moving. Someone's up there.

527
00:59:42,571 --> 00:59:44,491
People from the senior center?

528
00:59:51,031 --> 00:59:52,281
It's gone.

529
00:59:52,281 --> 00:59:53,871
That's the peak road.

530
00:59:57,661 --> 00:59:59,501
Sousuke, stay there with Ponyo.

531
01:00:11,091 --> 01:00:14,811
Maybe I could get through on the mountain road.

532
01:00:17,981 --> 01:00:20,601
Sousuke, I'm going to the senior center.

533
01:00:20,601 --> 01:00:21,811
I'll go too.

534
01:00:23,021 --> 01:00:25,071
Stay here with Ponyo.

535
01:00:25,071 --> 01:00:28,651
I'm going too. Let's take Ponyo with us.

536
01:00:29,321 --> 01:00:30,821
I'm going with you!

537
01:00:33,071 --> 01:00:36,951
Sousuke, our house is a lighthouse in the storm.

538
01:00:36,951 --> 01:00:41,121
Everyone out there is depending on us.

539
01:00:41,121 --> 01:00:43,081
Someone has to stay here.

540
01:00:44,041 --> 01:00:48,841
Lots of things are happening that I don't understand.

541
01:00:48,841 --> 01:00:53,261
But right now I'm worried about the people at the senior center.

542
01:00:53,851 --> 01:00:58,351
Just knowing you're here will help me.

543
01:00:58,351 --> 01:01:01,351
Don't worry. I promise to come back.

544
01:01:02,851 --> 01:01:03,861
Promise?

545
01:01:05,231 --> 01:01:06,781
I promise.

546
01:01:06,781 --> 01:01:08,151
You promised!

547
01:01:09,241 --> 01:01:10,861
I love you, Sousuke.

548
01:02:05,581 --> 01:02:09,171
I see the lights of the town!

549
01:02:09,171 --> 01:02:10,171
Finally...

550
01:02:10,591 --> 01:02:12,551
Now we can navigate.

551
01:02:12,551 --> 01:02:14,681
I've never seen that town before.

552
01:02:20,311 --> 01:02:23,561
Did the storm blow us to America?

553
01:02:41,291 --> 01:02:44,461
That's not a mountain. And that's no harbor...

554
01:02:44,961 --> 01:02:46,331
Those are ships!

555
01:02:56,381 --> 01:02:59,221
The sea is piled up into a mountain!

556
01:03:00,011 --> 01:03:02,011
It's a ship graveyard.

557
01:03:02,011 --> 01:03:04,101
What's going on?

558
01:03:09,311 --> 01:03:10,901
We lost power!

559
01:03:10,901 --> 01:03:14,031
Heave to! Drop the sea anchor!

560
01:03:14,031 --> 01:03:14,741
Aye, aye!

561
01:03:28,461 --> 01:03:30,291
Something is coming!

562
01:03:58,281 --> 01:03:59,861
A sea goddess?!

563
01:04:10,671 --> 01:04:11,751
The engine!

564
01:04:11,751 --> 01:04:12,961
We're saved!

565
01:04:12,961 --> 01:04:16,251
The engine started again. It was Her!

566
01:04:16,251 --> 01:04:19,801
Protect us from harm...

567
01:04:47,081 --> 01:04:48,331
Come on, come on.

568
01:05:02,221 --> 01:05:04,721
A barrier spell!

569
01:05:04,721 --> 01:05:07,181
Where did she learn this?

570
01:05:24,781 --> 01:05:26,281
Good heavens...

571
01:05:26,281 --> 01:05:28,081
She's human!

572
01:05:28,621 --> 01:05:31,661
Hey, watch out! What are you doing?

573
01:05:39,711 --> 01:05:42,461
Stop! This is dangerous!

574
01:05:45,471 --> 01:05:46,971
Stop that at once!

575
01:05:54,561 --> 01:05:57,811
I'm simply trying to save your sister.

576
01:06:03,241 --> 01:06:06,161
She's here. She answered my call!

577
01:06:43,071 --> 01:06:44,441
Fujimoto...

578
01:06:44,441 --> 01:06:46,441
You came, my beloved.

579
01:06:47,531 --> 01:06:49,161
Such a beautiful ocean.

580
01:06:53,291 --> 01:06:58,291
So full of magic, like my ancient Devonian sea.

581
01:06:58,711 --> 01:07:01,131
It's Ponyo! She tasted human blood...

582
01:07:01,131 --> 01:07:04,381
...and plundered all of my elixir.

583
01:07:05,091 --> 01:07:06,211
Ponyo...

584
01:07:06,671 --> 01:07:08,761
What a lovely name.

585
01:07:14,601 --> 01:07:16,391
It's all my fault.

586
01:07:16,981 --> 01:07:21,481
She's totally beyond my control. It's a complete mess.

587
01:07:21,481 --> 01:07:24,231
She doesn't understand what she's done.

588
01:07:24,651 --> 01:07:29,991
Now she's human, and she's up there with her boyfriend!

589
01:07:30,781 --> 01:07:34,121
If we don't stop her, the planet is doomed!

590
01:07:43,251 --> 01:07:46,171
No! The satellites are falling.

591
01:07:46,171 --> 01:07:48,591
Earth's gravitational field...

592
01:07:49,721 --> 01:07:51,301
Be still...

593
01:07:58,851 --> 01:08:02,651
Sousuke... That is his name, yes?

594
01:08:06,271 --> 01:08:09,821
You love your sister, don't you?

595
01:08:13,571 --> 01:08:17,161
Listen, dear... What if Ponyo really became human?

596
01:08:17,991 --> 01:08:20,001
Use the old magic.

597
01:08:20,001 --> 01:08:24,831
If Sousuke's love is real, she'll lose her powers forever.

598
01:08:24,831 --> 01:08:29,591
But if it's not, she'll turn to sea foam!

599
01:08:30,011 --> 01:08:33,931
That's where we all came from, dear.

600
01:08:33,931 --> 01:08:36,721
But he's only five. That's impossible!

601
01:08:42,101 --> 01:08:45,691
Sleep well, little children.

602
01:08:58,831 --> 01:08:59,951
Sousuke!

603
01:09:01,411 --> 01:09:02,831
Sousuke!

604
01:09:03,911 --> 01:09:05,331
Ow!

605
01:09:08,091 --> 01:09:09,801
Good morning, Ponyo.

606
01:09:09,801 --> 01:09:12,301
Morning, Sousuke.

607
01:09:18,681 --> 01:09:21,061
We almost got flooded.

608
01:09:44,661 --> 01:09:46,621
Where's Lisa?

609
01:09:46,621 --> 01:09:48,921
She must be stuck someplace.

610
01:09:49,881 --> 01:09:51,961
I wish we had a boat.

611
01:09:54,881 --> 01:09:56,471
There's a boat!

612
01:09:58,681 --> 01:09:59,971
We can't fit.

613
01:09:59,971 --> 01:10:01,351
Can so.

614
01:10:17,361 --> 01:10:18,531
Awesome!

615
01:10:21,571 --> 01:10:23,621
The candle's bigger too.

616
01:10:23,621 --> 01:10:24,951
We can fit.

617
01:10:24,951 --> 01:10:26,501
This is cool.

618
01:10:26,501 --> 01:10:27,871
Cool!

619
01:10:27,871 --> 01:10:29,211
Grab that end.

620
01:10:32,881 --> 01:10:34,341
Ready?

621
01:10:34,341 --> 01:10:35,711
Ready!

622
01:10:48,641 --> 01:10:50,061
She's seaworthy!

623
01:10:52,611 --> 01:10:55,191
Awesome. No leaks!

624
01:10:55,191 --> 01:10:57,691
Now we fill the boiler.

625
01:10:58,401 --> 01:11:00,361
The water goes in here.

626
01:11:01,281 --> 01:11:03,661
It goes in the boiler.

627
01:11:31,311 --> 01:11:32,771
It's like a rocket!

628
01:11:40,151 --> 01:11:41,861
Everything's shipshape.

629
01:11:41,861 --> 01:11:43,071
Shipshape...

630
01:11:44,111 --> 01:11:45,201
Shipshape?

631
01:11:45,201 --> 01:11:46,201
Shipshape!

632
01:11:46,201 --> 01:11:50,701
Shipshape! Shipshape!

633
01:12:11,981 --> 01:12:13,271
Is it hot?

634
01:12:13,271 --> 01:12:14,271
Hot!

635
01:12:18,521 --> 01:12:19,231
Hot!

636
01:12:19,231 --> 01:12:20,651
It's hot.

637
01:12:24,031 --> 01:12:25,411
The candle's burning.

638
01:12:25,411 --> 01:12:26,911
It's burning!

639
01:12:26,911 --> 01:12:29,991
Hot! Hot! Hot!

640
01:12:37,881 --> 01:12:39,501
It's hot.

641
01:12:50,601 --> 01:12:52,181
Awesome!

642
01:12:53,851 --> 01:12:56,811
We're shipshape, Sousuke!

643
01:12:56,811 --> 01:12:58,771
This is great.

644
01:13:06,151 --> 01:13:08,281
This is so much fun.

645
01:13:09,451 --> 01:13:12,121
It's burning, Sousuke.

646
01:13:12,581 --> 01:13:14,701
It's really hot.

647
01:13:15,461 --> 01:13:17,501
Keep a lookout in front.

648
01:13:17,501 --> 01:13:19,211
I'll steer the boat.

649
01:13:19,631 --> 01:13:21,541
Okay, I'm the lookout.

650
01:13:48,451 --> 01:13:50,071
There's a road.

651
01:13:50,071 --> 01:13:52,161
That's the road Lisa took.

652
01:13:54,581 --> 01:13:56,581
I don't see her.

653
01:13:56,581 --> 01:13:59,791
You will. She gave me her promise.

654
01:14:04,881 --> 01:14:08,171
Ancient fish... from the Devonian age!

655
01:14:08,171 --> 01:14:10,341
There's Bothriolepis.

656
01:14:15,471 --> 01:14:16,811
That one is...

657
01:14:16,811 --> 01:14:17,891
Dipnorhynchus.

658
01:14:17,891 --> 01:14:19,441
Dipnorhynchus!

659
01:14:20,651 --> 01:14:22,151
That one's really huge.

660
01:14:22,151 --> 01:14:24,021
That's Devonynchus.

661
01:14:24,021 --> 01:14:25,361
Devonynchus!

662
01:14:32,491 --> 01:14:34,581
Ahoy!

663
01:14:38,251 --> 01:14:39,121
A boat!

664
01:14:40,211 --> 01:14:41,871
Ahoy!

665
01:14:43,081 --> 01:14:44,541
They're calling us.

666
01:14:45,921 --> 01:14:48,381
Ahoy!

667
01:14:49,591 --> 01:14:50,511
Ow!

668
01:14:58,141 --> 01:14:59,521
Pretty good, huh?

669
01:15:03,191 --> 01:15:04,691
Now, Ponyo.

670
01:15:11,071 --> 01:15:13,411
Hello.

671
01:15:13,411 --> 01:15:16,201
That's a wonderful boat you have.

672
01:15:16,201 --> 01:15:19,291
It's Lisa's little boy, Sou-chan.

673
01:15:19,291 --> 01:15:22,251
It's Sousuke, not Sou-chan!

674
01:15:22,251 --> 01:15:23,461
This is Ponyo.

675
01:15:24,751 --> 01:15:26,921
I was a fish before.

676
01:15:26,921 --> 01:15:28,381
A fish?

677
01:15:29,511 --> 01:15:31,421
Ponyo... That's a nice name.

678
01:15:33,681 --> 01:15:35,841
Mister, have you seen Lisa?

679
01:15:35,841 --> 01:15:36,931
Lisa-san?

680
01:15:38,141 --> 01:15:39,931
She's not with you?

681
01:15:39,931 --> 01:15:41,391
She's at the center.

682
01:15:41,391 --> 01:15:42,931
The senior center?

683
01:15:42,931 --> 01:15:44,441
This is my baby.

684
01:16:14,341 --> 01:16:16,641
Oh, my. What happened?

685
01:16:22,771 --> 01:16:24,681
Is that for us?

686
01:16:38,451 --> 01:16:39,821
Give me the cup, dear.

687
01:16:45,041 --> 01:16:46,331
Thank you.

688
01:16:46,751 --> 01:16:48,501
Let's try it.

689
01:16:52,381 --> 01:16:54,051
Delicious soup!

690
01:16:54,631 --> 01:16:56,171
Lisa made it.

691
01:16:56,921 --> 01:16:58,341
It's for the baby.

692
01:16:58,971 --> 01:17:03,851
Oh, I'm sorry. He can't handle soup yet.

693
01:17:04,271 --> 01:17:08,351
But this will help me make milk for him.

694
01:17:10,521 --> 01:17:12,861
Lisa gave me her milk too.

695
01:17:13,401 --> 01:17:16,741
Ponyo, may I have this?

696
01:17:16,741 --> 01:17:18,571
Sure.

697
01:17:19,161 --> 01:17:20,161
Thank you.

698
01:17:37,841 --> 01:17:39,721
People from the town.

699
01:17:39,721 --> 01:17:41,391
It's like a festival.

700
01:17:41,841 --> 01:17:46,271
You there! Do you need assistance?

701
01:17:46,681 --> 01:17:51,521
Thanks, we're okay right now!

702
01:17:52,021 --> 01:17:54,821
Then please follow us.

703
01:17:54,821 --> 01:17:57,941
We're going to the hotel on the peak.

704
01:17:57,941 --> 01:18:00,571
Okay! Will do.

705
01:18:02,281 --> 01:18:04,121
The whole town's here.

706
01:18:04,121 --> 01:18:06,791
I hope everyone's all right...

707
01:18:06,791 --> 01:18:08,201
Let's go, Ponyo.

708
01:18:08,201 --> 01:18:10,331
Hold on a second.

709
01:18:15,961 --> 01:18:17,001
Milk!

710
01:18:17,921 --> 01:18:18,761
Oh, my...

711
01:18:20,261 --> 01:18:21,631
Milk!

712
01:18:21,631 --> 01:18:24,301
She ate up all the ham.

713
01:18:24,301 --> 01:18:27,351
Thank you. This will help me make good milk.

714
01:18:27,351 --> 01:18:31,601
Can you use another candle for your boat, Sousuke-kun?

715
01:18:31,601 --> 01:18:34,311
Yeah. Ponyo will make it bigger.

716
01:18:34,311 --> 01:18:35,561
Thanks.

717
01:18:36,151 --> 01:18:37,111
Be careful!

718
01:18:37,111 --> 01:18:38,361
Thank you both!

719
01:18:44,781 --> 01:18:45,951
What is it, dear?

720
01:18:50,791 --> 01:18:52,121
Don't cry.

721
01:19:11,391 --> 01:19:12,771
Ponyo!

722
01:19:25,861 --> 01:19:27,121
Sou-chan!

723
01:19:27,121 --> 01:19:27,871
It's Sou-chan!

724
01:19:27,871 --> 01:19:28,451
Amazing!

725
01:19:28,451 --> 01:19:29,331
Looks cool!

726
01:19:29,331 --> 01:19:32,451
Where's Lisa-san? Isn't she with you?

727
01:19:32,451 --> 01:19:35,711
I'm going to pick her up.

728
01:19:35,711 --> 01:19:39,341
So she survived that wave?

729
01:19:39,841 --> 01:19:42,461
Sousuke, take me with you!

730
01:19:42,841 --> 01:19:45,551
Later, Kumiko-chan. I'm busy right now.

731
01:19:45,551 --> 01:19:49,391
Everyone from the center evacuated to the park.

732
01:19:49,391 --> 01:19:50,221
Take care!

733
01:19:50,221 --> 01:19:51,641
You can do it!

734
01:19:52,141 --> 01:19:55,851
We'll send a boat for them later.

735
01:19:55,851 --> 01:19:58,101
Good luck, captain!

736
01:20:47,241 --> 01:20:49,951
Time for a new candle, Ponyo.

737
01:20:53,951 --> 01:20:56,911
We're okay. I have another one.

738
01:20:57,791 --> 01:20:58,661
Ow!

739
01:20:59,291 --> 01:21:00,791
It's still pretty hot.

740
01:21:05,921 --> 01:21:08,221
Bye-bye.

741
01:21:09,471 --> 01:21:12,971
Can you make this candle bigger?

742
01:21:12,971 --> 01:21:14,181
All right.

743
01:21:20,021 --> 01:21:22,941
Are you sleepy, Ponyo?

744
01:21:30,071 --> 01:21:30,991
Ponyo!

745
01:21:47,171 --> 01:21:48,961
Ponyo! Ponyo!

746
01:22:46,771 --> 01:22:49,151
Good... It's shallow enough to walk.

747
01:23:15,801 --> 01:23:17,091
A road!

748
01:23:29,611 --> 01:23:30,941
It's shrinking!

749
01:23:32,861 --> 01:23:33,781
Ponyo!

750
01:23:53,841 --> 01:23:54,761
Ponyo!

751
01:23:56,091 --> 01:23:58,181
Ponyo, wake up!

752
01:24:00,801 --> 01:24:02,471
Sousuke...

753
01:24:08,481 --> 01:24:09,811
I'm relieved.

754
01:24:10,231 --> 01:24:12,981
I thought you were turning into a fish.

755
01:24:25,581 --> 01:24:26,541
Lisa's car!

756
01:24:26,541 --> 01:24:28,831
Ponyo, that's her car!

757
01:24:32,921 --> 01:24:34,381
Lisa!

758
01:24:34,921 --> 01:24:35,551
Lisa!

759
01:24:38,131 --> 01:24:39,131
Lisa!

760
01:24:39,801 --> 01:24:40,761
Lisa!

761
01:24:43,101 --> 01:24:44,601
Lisa!

762
01:24:47,021 --> 01:24:48,561
Lisa!

763
01:24:50,021 --> 01:24:50,941
Lisa!

764
01:24:53,401 --> 01:24:54,271
Lisa!

765
01:24:56,981 --> 01:24:58,991
Lisa!

766
01:25:02,031 --> 01:25:03,661
Lisa!

767
01:25:32,101 --> 01:25:34,561
Here's your boat.

768
01:25:34,561 --> 01:25:36,981
Your eyes are wet.

769
01:25:44,201 --> 01:25:45,871
Let's find Lisa.

770
01:26:33,201 --> 01:26:34,291
You forgot your wrap!

771
01:26:34,291 --> 01:26:36,461
Who needs it?

772
01:26:36,461 --> 01:26:37,711
Hurry up!

773
01:26:37,711 --> 01:26:39,501
Look, it's a whale!

774
01:26:42,261 --> 01:26:43,591
My knees don't hurt anymore!

775
01:26:43,591 --> 01:26:45,631
What were we so afraid of?

776
01:26:45,631 --> 01:26:46,591
Is this the Other Side?

777
01:26:46,591 --> 01:26:48,591
Who cares? It's wonderful.

778
01:26:51,351 --> 01:26:54,481
Attention, please! Gather around.

779
01:26:54,481 --> 01:26:56,191
Coming!

780
01:26:56,191 --> 01:26:57,941
Shall we?

781
01:26:59,901 --> 01:27:02,231
It's so nice to run.

782
01:27:02,231 --> 01:27:04,401
Meet you there!

783
01:27:07,321 --> 01:27:08,861
The winner!

784
01:27:11,241 --> 01:27:13,411
You're so fast, Kayo-san.

785
01:27:14,451 --> 01:27:16,211
Quiet, everyone!

786
01:27:16,961 --> 01:27:19,331
The moment of truth is at hand.

787
01:27:19,331 --> 01:27:22,171
Sousuke-kun and Ponyo are almost here.

788
01:27:22,171 --> 01:27:23,711
It's so romantic.

789
01:27:23,711 --> 01:27:25,131
Will love triumph?

790
01:27:25,131 --> 01:27:26,881
I'm so excited!

791
01:27:29,341 --> 01:27:30,761
Quiet!

792
01:27:30,761 --> 01:27:33,561
Very soon, you will bear witness to a sacred trial of love.

793
01:27:33,561 --> 01:27:35,771
I'm asking you to wait patiently.

794
01:27:37,271 --> 01:27:41,941
Fujimoto-san, you're not up to something, are you?

795
01:27:41,941 --> 01:27:42,941
I hope not!

796
01:27:42,941 --> 01:27:44,151
Nonsense.

797
01:27:44,151 --> 01:27:44,981
He's her father.

798
01:27:44,981 --> 01:27:46,281
They'll be fine...

799
01:27:47,401 --> 01:27:49,531
...if she doesn't wake up.

800
01:27:49,531 --> 01:27:50,321
Now excuse me!

801
01:27:59,501 --> 01:28:01,961
I'd like to believe him...

802
01:28:01,961 --> 01:28:04,541
Where's Lisa-san gone to?

803
01:28:04,541 --> 01:28:09,341
She's been talking with Ponyo's mother for ages.

804
01:28:17,311 --> 01:28:20,061
I hope she's okay.

805
01:28:20,061 --> 01:28:22,351
What are they talking about?

806
01:28:22,771 --> 01:28:25,611
Let's find out. Lisa-san!

807
01:28:25,611 --> 01:28:28,861
Lisa-san!

808
01:28:34,241 --> 01:28:41,461
We're all rooting for Sousuke and Ponyo!

809
01:28:54,681 --> 01:28:55,971
Lisa-san!

810
01:28:55,971 --> 01:28:57,351
You must be worried.

811
01:28:57,351 --> 01:28:59,601
Sou-chan will be fine.

812
01:28:59,601 --> 01:29:02,311
He's a strong little boy.

813
01:29:03,231 --> 01:29:06,271
Thanks, everyone. He'll need your support.

814
01:29:15,531 --> 01:29:17,371
Ponyo, it's a tunnel.

815
01:29:21,251 --> 01:29:28,591
Note: STOP

816
01:29:33,171 --> 01:29:35,341
I've been here before.

817
01:29:36,431 --> 01:29:37,391
Ponyo?

818
01:29:37,971 --> 01:29:39,681
I don't like this place.

819
01:29:44,061 --> 01:29:45,811
Don't let go of my hand.

820
01:30:23,971 --> 01:30:24,931
Ponyo!

821
01:30:44,831 --> 01:30:45,541
Ponyo!

822
01:30:53,881 --> 01:30:54,881
Ponyo!

823
01:31:16,651 --> 01:31:19,151
Please don't die!

824
01:31:19,571 --> 01:31:20,701
Ponyo!

825
01:31:21,781 --> 01:31:24,411
Wake up, Ponyo!

826
01:31:25,621 --> 01:31:27,001
Let her sleep.

827
01:31:28,331 --> 01:31:30,461
I've been waiting for you, Sousuke-kun.

828
01:31:30,461 --> 01:31:33,791
Lisa-san and the old ladies are waiting too.

829
01:31:34,751 --> 01:31:35,801
Lisa?!

830
01:31:35,801 --> 01:31:39,421
Won't you come with me? You and Ponyo.

831
01:31:42,141 --> 01:31:45,101
Let's not wake her up.

832
01:31:45,101 --> 01:31:46,721
Sousuke!

833
01:31:47,471 --> 01:31:50,521
Don't listen to him!

834
01:31:51,061 --> 01:31:54,401
He tricked everyone into going with him.

835
01:31:54,401 --> 01:31:55,441
Toki-san!

836
01:31:55,441 --> 01:31:57,401
But he couldn't fool me!

837
01:31:58,111 --> 01:32:01,151
There's no time, I tell you.

838
01:32:01,911 --> 01:32:03,781
Don't you see what's happening?

839
01:32:03,781 --> 01:32:07,411
If the Moon comes any closer, we're finished!

840
01:32:07,411 --> 01:32:10,791
Liar! Is that the best you can do?

841
01:32:11,291 --> 01:32:13,751
Sousuke, come here!

842
01:32:13,751 --> 01:32:17,881
Listen to me, Sousuke-kun. You're the planet's last hope.

843
01:32:17,881 --> 01:32:19,381
Don't make me use force.

844
01:32:20,761 --> 01:32:21,671
Ponyo!

845
01:32:24,051 --> 01:32:26,221
Is this how you treat your father?

846
01:32:32,601 --> 01:32:34,311
Ponyo!

847
01:32:34,311 --> 01:32:37,151
Run, Sousuke!

848
01:32:37,151 --> 01:32:38,941
You don't understand!

849
01:32:44,321 --> 01:32:46,161
You can make it!

850
01:32:48,161 --> 01:32:49,661
Jump!

851
01:33:29,281 --> 01:33:30,281
Now what?

852
01:34:25,421 --> 01:34:26,301
Lisa!

853
01:34:26,301 --> 01:34:27,631
Sousuke!

854
01:34:27,631 --> 01:34:28,551
Ponyo!

855
01:34:33,811 --> 01:34:35,181
Look over there.

856
01:34:35,181 --> 01:34:37,391
Where are we?

857
01:34:47,781 --> 01:34:49,611
So you are Sousuke-san.

858
01:34:50,071 --> 01:34:51,241
Hello.

859
01:34:51,701 --> 01:34:53,241
Are you Ponyo's mother?

860
01:34:53,781 --> 01:34:54,701
Yes.

861
01:34:55,161 --> 01:34:59,711
I want to thank you for bringing my daughter back to me.

862
01:35:00,251 --> 01:35:01,751
Sousuke-san...

863
01:35:01,751 --> 01:35:05,801
Ponyo wanted to be like you, but she unleashed a terrible power.

864
01:35:06,801 --> 01:35:10,801
To become human, she must be loved...

865
01:35:10,801 --> 01:35:13,801
...for who she really is.

866
01:35:14,261 --> 01:35:18,391
Do you know that Ponyo was a fish?

867
01:35:18,811 --> 01:35:19,641
Yes.

868
01:35:19,641 --> 01:35:23,731
Your blood made her almost human.

869
01:35:23,731 --> 01:35:24,901
That's right!

870
01:35:24,901 --> 01:35:28,401
Ponyo licked my cut and made it better.

871
01:35:28,401 --> 01:35:30,951
So that's why she changed!

872
01:35:31,991 --> 01:35:35,701
Can you accept her as she is?

873
01:35:35,701 --> 01:35:38,161
I'll always love Ponyo...

874
01:35:38,161 --> 01:35:40,911
...whether she's a fish, a human...

875
01:35:40,911 --> 01:35:42,421
...or in between.

876
01:35:56,641 --> 01:35:59,061
Come, Ponyo.

877
01:36:13,241 --> 01:36:18,161
Ponyo, Sousuke-san has promised to accept you as you are.

878
01:36:20,871 --> 01:36:24,671
But first, you must give up your powers.

879
01:36:25,121 --> 01:36:26,211
Can you do that?

880
01:36:36,971 --> 01:36:40,851
Kiss this bubble when you return to land...

881
01:36:40,851 --> 01:36:44,811
...and Ponyo will be a little girl.

882
01:36:47,981 --> 01:36:50,111
Way to go, Ponyo!

883
01:36:50,981 --> 01:36:53,401
Thank you, Ponyo's mother!

884
01:36:59,531 --> 01:37:03,201
Now the planet is safe again.

885
01:37:06,251 --> 01:37:08,461
Splendid, Sou-chan!

886
01:37:08,461 --> 01:37:10,041
Sousuke!

887
01:37:10,711 --> 01:37:12,301
Sousuke!

888
01:37:14,551 --> 01:37:16,091
Sousuke!

889
01:37:40,201 --> 01:37:42,121
I'm grateful, Lisa.

890
01:37:42,491 --> 01:37:45,201
Thank you, Gran Mamare.

891
01:37:56,631 --> 01:37:59,471
Is everyone all right?

892
01:38:04,511 --> 01:38:06,891
Wait, I'll get the wheelchairs.

893
01:38:06,891 --> 01:38:09,141
Don't bother. We'll walk.

894
01:38:09,141 --> 01:38:11,351
It's all so exciting.

895
01:38:14,861 --> 01:38:16,691
I believe this is yours.

896
01:38:19,111 --> 01:38:20,201
Thanks.

897
01:38:20,701 --> 01:38:22,571
I hope you'll forgive me...

898
01:38:22,571 --> 01:38:24,701
Um... May I?

899
01:38:30,371 --> 01:38:31,961
Take good care of her.

900
01:38:34,751 --> 01:38:36,131
It's Koichi!

901
01:38:40,841 --> 01:38:42,391
Koichi!

902
01:38:46,221 --> 01:38:49,391
It's Lisa! And there's Sousuke!

903
01:38:52,101 --> 01:38:54,311
Look, Ponyo. It's Koichi!

904
01:39:15,961 --> 01:39:19,761
Ponyo Ponyo Ponyo, tiny little fish

905
01:39:19,761 --> 01:39:23,971
She's a little fish from the deep blue sea

906
01:39:23,971 --> 01:39:27,721
Ponyo Ponyo Ponyo, she's a little girl

907
01:39:27,721 --> 01:39:31,771
She's a little girl with a round tummy

908
01:39:39,941 --> 01:39:43,991
Pitter patter, hop hop and jump

909
01:39:43,991 --> 01:39:47,991
Look, I have legs! I'm gonna run!

910
01:39:47,991 --> 01:39:51,951
Squishy squeeze, wave them around

911
01:39:51,951 --> 01:39:55,871
Look, I have hands! Let's hold them now!

912
01:39:56,211 --> 01:40:00,211
When I'm skipping with him

913
01:40:00,211 --> 01:40:03,971
My heart does this dance

914
01:40:03,971 --> 01:40:07,971
Munch, munch! Kiss, hug!

915
01:40:08,431 --> 01:40:13,981
Oh, he's my favorite little boy

916
01:40:13,981 --> 01:40:15,981
Rosy rosy red red

917
01:40:15,981 --> 01:40:19,731
Ponyo Ponyo Ponyo, tiny little fish

918
01:40:19,731 --> 01:40:23,941
She's a little fish from the deep blue sea

919
01:40:23,941 --> 01:40:27,701
Ponyo Ponyo Ponyo, she's a little girl

920
01:40:27,701 --> 01:40:31,791
She's a little girl with a round tummy

921
01:40:32,291 --> 01:40:38,291
Studio Ghibli

922
01:40:39,421 --> 01:40:46,681
The End

